      "hints": [
        "Set up $\\int_0^2 (\\frac{1}{2}x^3 - \\frac{7}{2}x^2 + 5x)\\,dx$.",
        "Integrate: $[\\frac{x^4}{8} - \\frac{7x^3}{6} + \\frac{5x^2}{2}]_0^2$.",
        "Evaluate at $x = 2$: $2 - \\frac{28}{3} + 10 = \\frac{8}{3}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Set up the integral for the area between the curve and the line $y = x$ from $x = 0$ to $x = 2$:\n$$\\text{Area} = \\int_0^2 \\left[ \\frac{1}{2}(x^3 - 7x^2 + 12x) - x \\right]\\,dx = \\int_0^2 \\left( \\frac{1}{2}x^3 - \\frac{7}{2}x^2 + 5x \\right)\\,dx$$",
        "Integrate term-by-term:\n$$\\text{Area} = \\left[ \\frac{x^4}{8} - \\frac{7x^3}{6} + \\frac{5x^2}{2} \\right]_0^2$$",
        "Evaluate between the limits $x = 0$ and $x = 2$:\n$$\\text{Area} = \\left( \\frac{2^4}{8} - \\frac{7(2^3)}{6} + \\frac{5(2^2)}{2} \\right) - 0 = 2 - \\frac{28}{3} + 10 = 12 - \\frac{28}{3} = \\frac{8}{3} \\quad \\left(\\text{or } 2\\frac{2}{3} \\approx 2.67\\right)$$"
      ],
